# MojoLlama — Coding Memory

## Goal
Build a Mojo-based LLM inference server (MojoLlama) with native GGUF support, starting with an MVP that can load GGUF files and run inference.

## Constraints & Preferences
- Mojo SDK version 0.26.2.0 installed via `uv pip install --system mojo`
- Target model: Qwen2.5-0.5B GGUF (396MB file, 630M params, 291 tensors, 24 layers)
- Python interop requires `LD_PRELOAD=/opt/conda/lib/libpython3.12.so.1.0`
- `main()` cannot take arguments; use `MODEL_PATH` env var
- No file-scope enums, `match`, `DynamicVector`, or `List` in Mojo 0.26
- System RAM: ~7.8GB total, ~2.6GB available, no swap — memory-constrained
- Python inference module uses `gguf` library, `numpy`, `regex`, and `ftfy`
- Bash tool default timeout 120s — must override for test scripts >2 min

